From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: mmdevapi: a standard user keeps the audio device registry in their own hive

mmdevapi kept its endpoint registry (device GUIDs, state, properties) only
in HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\MMDevices\Audio and opened
it for writing. A standard user may not write HKLM, so on the shared machine
prefix load_devices_from_reg failed ("Couldn't create key: 5"), no endpoint
had a property store (OpenPropKey "failed with 6"), and the device list
changed from one enumeration to the next: Audacity 4, as a standard user,
sized its device table from one enumeration, filled it from another, overran
it and crashed at start. Each user's session finds its own audio devices, so
when HKLM is not writable the registry is kept under
HKCU\Software\Wine\MMDevices\Audio instead.

Gate: make test-mmdevkey (HKLM's key read-only, every active endpoint must
still have its name).
--- a/dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c
+++ b/dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c
@@ -462,6 +462,15 @@
     ret = RegCreateKeyExW(HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE,
             L"Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\MMDevices\\Audio", 0, NULL, 0,
             KEY_WRITE|KEY_READ|KEY_WOW64_64KEY, NULL, &root, NULL);
+    /* Stained Glass OS: a standard user may not write the machine's device
+     * registry (HKLM), and each user's session finds its own audio devices:
+     * keep that user's device registry in the user's own hive instead of
+     * running with none -- without it the endpoints had no properties and the
+     * device list changed from one enumeration to the next (Audacity 4, as a
+     * standard user on the shared machine prefix, overran its device table). */
+    if (ret == ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED)
+        ret = RegCreateKeyExW(HKEY_CURRENT_USER, L"Software\\Wine\\MMDevices\\Audio", 0, NULL, 0,
+                KEY_WRITE|KEY_READ|KEY_WOW64_64KEY, NULL, &root, NULL);
     if (ret == ERROR_SUCCESS)
         ret = RegCreateKeyExW(root, L"Capture", 0, NULL, 0, KEY_READ|KEY_WRITE|KEY_WOW64_64KEY, NULL, &key_capture, NULL);
     if (ret == ERROR_SUCCESS)
